    "External R4STD static Zig owner: Unicode17.0.0/UAX29rev47 default extended graphemes, GB3-GB999 including Indic GB9c, EP/Extend/ZWJ GB11 and odd RI parity. Generated sorted pinned GCB/InCB/EP ranges, algorithmic complete Hangul LV/LVT. Original data/license/hash URLs retained; offline PowerShell7 regeneration and pinned Zig formatting byte-exact.",
    "Allocation-free scalar state/strict UTF8 iterator/stream events and complete-input bounded-prefix/floor/ceil/previous/next helpers. Stream retains at most four pending UTF8 bytes; caller owns arbitrary-length cluster bytes until next boundary/EOF. Full invalid suffixes never pass as safe bounded prefixes.",
    "SDK57 TextField/TextArea cursor/selection/Backspace/Delete/mouse hit and line wrap follow cluster boundaries. Selection replacement preflights full UTF8 and whole-cluster capacity before deleting old bytes. Typed insertion can merge following combining text; cursor snaps after the complete new cluster. Labels/ellipsis clips remain presentation only and keep full clusters.",
    "12 actual shared-widget apps and Terminal rebuilt/versioned, direct Library dependencies and Distribution host package pins aligned to23/SDK57 to keep one forked identity. Full codepoints at Services/AppDefaults/NetConfig/RegEdit/LogCenter/Appearance/Klickifax/Example input edges instead of low-byte aliases. Existing exact filename/path identities and create-only save behavior retained.",
    "Notepad/R4Code prepare one bounded file candidate, independent of512-byte I/O chunk boundaries. Invalid complete UTF8 preserves the old visible document. One lookahead byte can prove a preceding boundary; the unproved final cluster/partial scalar at a truncated tail stays out. Existing truncated-source save restrictions remain.",
    "Terminal command Backspace removes an entire Unicode cluster and emits one erase per existing printable scalar cell. History prefixes keep full clusters. /GRAPHEMETEST creates/joins/reaps the actual private console child, existing full queue/stale-target/typed+byte-stream loops now delete a real ZWJ sequence and verify exact history.",
    "Clipboard owner already rejects oversized writes and too-small reads; widgets read its entire4095-byte capacity. Thus the common paste source is not a silently clipped scalar prefix. No clipboard/kernel change was needed.",
    "Current font/console contract remains scalar glyph advances/fallbacks; cluster segmentation supplies neither zero-width combining marks, emoji shaping, bidirectional layout nor wide-cell negotiation. Shared editor wrap/hit positions keep complete clusters while scalar cell counts remain separate; existing malformed display-only fallback retained. Stock14font bytes and prior FontImport08540 evidence retained; no new glyph coverage claimed."
